# Trygon Predator ({1}{G}{U}, 2/3 flyer): "Whenever this creature deals combat damage to a player, you may destroy target
# artifact or enchantment that player controls." Bot2 controls a Forest, a Llanowar Elves, a Mox Pearl and a Sol Ring; Bot1
# controls its own Moxen. Turn 3 it connects: the Forest, the Elves and Bot1's own Mox Jet are not candidates (refused), Sol
# Ring is, and is destroyed. Bot2 then casts Fastbond (an enchantment). Turn 5 it connects again and targets Fastbond but
# Bot1 declines: it stays. Turn 7 Bot1 targets it again and accepts: it is destroyed. Bot2 takes 2 each time (20 to 14) and
# the Mox Pearl, never targeted, survives.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Trygon Predator
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Pearl
Llanowar Elves
Sol Ring
Fastbond
Forest x15

